IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nrsr-dates`

-- National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) -- baseline encoding from the seat of the
-- survivor: the person who was sexually abused as a child in circumstances an institution was responsible for, and who
-- applies for redress under the scheme. In Rules ss 34-35C the seat is the family member or other person asking what
-- notice they will get when the applicant dies.
--
-- SEAT. The survivor. The Operator, the institutions, the funders of last resort and the Ministers get no seat; their
-- findings ("considers", "is satisfied", "determines") are asked as facts, and their duties are encoded as what the
-- survivor must be given, or what may be done to them, and by when.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list); none takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
-- Two steps with a deadline are regulative rules run inside a question: Rules s 15(2) (the Operator's notice to a child
-- applicant, 3 to 6 months before turning 18) and Rules s 74(2) (my notice, before I accept my offer of redress, that I
-- have accepted a payment offer from a responsible institution).
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: Rules ss 4B, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 15, 17, 26(1)-(5) (and (6) as "not covered"), 31, 33, 34, 35,
-- 35A, 35B, 35C, 37, 39, 42, 43, 44-54A, 71, 72, 73, 74. What is out, and why, is in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018, Compilation No. 9, compilation date
-- 19 February 2025 (register id F2025C00180), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/F2018L00975.txt.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- (NOTES.md): an answer says "no" only where the Rules' own words say no; where a section simply does not reach the
-- facts, the answer says the section does not apply, and the Act decides.

§ `National Redress Scheme Rules 2018 -- the survivor`

DECLARE `Rules party` IS ONE OF `I, the survivor`, `the Operator`
DECLARE `Rules step` IS ONE OF
    `notify the Operator in writing that I accepted the payment offer`
    `give me the notice about turning 18` HAS `the day of the notice` IS A NUMBER

§§ `Am I eligible as a child migrant (Rules Part 1A)`

-- Rules s 4B(2) and s 10(1) use the same four conditions: "(a) the person arrived in Australia before 1984 as a child who
-- was sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution and, when the person arrived in Australia, there were not
-- any other members of the person's family in Australia except one or more children; and (b) either: (i) the person was
-- sent to Australia under a scheme carried out under the Empire Settlement Act 1922 (United Kingdom); or (ii) the person
-- became a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children)
-- Act 1946; and (c) the person became a ward of a participating State or participating Territory; and (d) the abuse
-- occurred while the person was a ward of the State or Territory."
GIVEN `the year I arrived` IS A NUMBER, `I was a child when I arrived` IS A BOOLEAN, `sent by an institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `no adult family here` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 4B(2)(a) -- I arrived before 1984 as an unaccompanied child migrant` `the year I arrived` `I was a child when I arrived` `sent by an institution` `no adult family here` IF
        `the year I arrived` LESS THAN 1984
    AND `I was a child when I arrived`
    AND `sent by an institution`
    AND `no adult family here`

DECLARE `Whether Rules s 4B makes me eligible` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am eligible for redress as a child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta (Rules s 4B; Act s 13(2)); Australian citizenship or permanent residence (Act s 13(1)(e)) is not one of its conditions`
    `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(a): I did not arrive before 1984 as a child sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution, with no family in Australia except children`
    `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(b): I was not sent under an Empire Settlement Act 1922 scheme, nor made a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946`
    `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(c)-(d): I did not become a ward of a participating State or Territory, or the abuse did not occur while I was its ward`
    `no, not under Rules s 4B(1)(a)-(d): the sexual abuse is not within the scope of the scheme, would attract no redress payment under the assessment framework, or no participating or listed institution is responsible for it`

-- Rules s 4B(1): "For the purposes of subsection 13(2) of the Act, a person is also eligible for redress under the scheme
-- if: (a) the person was sexually abused; and (b) the sexual abuse is within the scope of the scheme; and (c) the sexual
-- abuse is of a kind for which the maximum amount of redress payment ... would be more than nil; and (d) one or more of the
-- following are responsible for the abuse: (i) a participating institution; (ii) an institution that is listed for a
-- participating jurisdiction under section 164A, 164B or 164C of the Act (if a participating jurisdiction is an eligible
-- funding jurisdiction ...); and (e) subsection (2) applies to the person." A failed "if": the Rules' own no, for this
-- route only; Act s 13(1) is another route (the Act encoding asks it).
@export Am I eligible for redress as a former child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta, even if I am not an Australian citizen or permanent resident (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 4B)? Child migrants who arrived before 1984 without adult family, came under the Empire Settlement Act scheme or became wards under the overseas children or child guardianship laws, became wards of a participating State or Territory and were abused while wards are eligible on this route without the citizenship condition. A "no" here means only that this route does not apply; the general test in the Act may still make you eligible.
GIVEN `the year I arrived in Australia` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you arrived in Australia, for example 1952
      `I was a child when I arrived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when you arrived in Australia
      `I was sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent to Australia from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution (such as a charity, church body or government agency)
      `I had no family in Australia except children when I arrived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you arrived, no members of your family were in Australia other than one or more children (for example brothers or sisters who were also children)
      `I was sent under an Empire Settlement Act scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent to Australia under a scheme carried out under the Empire Settlement Act 1922 (United Kingdom)
      `I became a ward under the overseas children or guardianship laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946
      `I became a ward of a participating State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became a ward of a State or Territory that participates in the National Redress Scheme
      `the abuse occurred while I was that ward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were a ward of that State or Territory
      `the sexual abuse is within the scope of the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the sexual abuse is within the scope of the scheme: it happened while you were a child, before 1 July 2018, and in a participating State, a Territory or outside Australia (Act s 14; see also Rules s 6 for abuse by another child)
      `the redress payment for it would be more than nil` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the maximum redress payment for that kind of abuse under the assessment framework would be more than nil
      `a participating or listed institution is responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a participating institution, or an institution listed for a participating jurisdiction under Act s 164A, 164B or 164C with an eligible funding jurisdiction, is responsible for the abuse
GIVETH A `Whether Rules s 4B makes me eligible`
`Am I eligible as a child migrant question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`Rules s 4B(2)(a) -- I arrived before 1984 as an unaccompanied child migrant` `the year I arrived in Australia` `I was a child when I arrived` `I was sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution` `I had no family in Australia except children when I arrived`))
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(a): I did not arrive before 1984 as a child sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution, with no family in Australia except children`
           IF (NOT (`I was sent under an Empire Settlement Act scheme` OR `I became a ward under the overseas children or guardianship laws`))
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(b): I was not sent under an Empire Settlement Act 1922 scheme, nor made a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946`
           IF (NOT (`I became a ward of a participating State or Territory` AND `the abuse occurred while I was that ward`))
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 4B(2)(c)-(d): I did not become a ward of a participating State or Territory, or the abuse did not occur while I was its ward`
           IF (NOT (`the sexual abuse is within the scope of the scheme` AND `the redress payment for it would be more than nil` AND `a participating or listed institution is responsible`))
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 4B(1)(a)-(d): the sexual abuse is not within the scope of the scheme, would attract no redress payment under the assessment framework, or no participating or listed institution is responsible for it`
           OTHERWISE `yes: I am eligible for redress as a child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta (Rules s 4B; Act s 13(2)); Australian citizenship or permanent residence (Act s 13(1)(e)) is not one of its conditions`

§§ `Is the abuse within the scope (Rules Part 2)`

DECLARE `Whether Rules s 6 takes the abuse out of the scope` IS ONE OF
    `out of the scope: sexual abuse by another child that involved neither physical contact with me nor penetration of me is not within the scope of the scheme (Rules s 6)`
    `Rules s 6 does not take it out: the abuser was not a child; whether it is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
    `Rules s 6 does not take it out: the abuse involved physical contact or penetration; whether it is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
    `Rules s 6 does not take it out: it speaks only of sexual abuse; whether non-sexual abuse is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`

-- Rules s 6: "For the purposes of subsection 14(3) of the Act, sexual abuse of a person by a child is not within the scope
-- of the scheme if the abuse did not involve physical contact with, or penetration of, the person."
@export Does it count under the redress scheme if the person who sexually abused me was also a child (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 6)? Sexual abuse by another child is outside the scheme if it involved no physical contact with you and no penetration. Abuse that did involve contact or penetration is not excluded by this rule; the Act's general test (when, where, and before 1 July 2018) still decides.
GIVEN `the abuse was sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse you are asking about was sexual abuse
      `the abuser was a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who abused you was under 18 at the time
      `the abuse involved physical contact or penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse involved physical contact with you, or penetration of you
GIVETH A `Whether Rules s 6 takes the abuse out of the scope`
`Does abuse by another child count question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the abuse was sexual abuse`)
              THEN `Rules s 6 does not take it out: it speaks only of sexual abuse; whether non-sexual abuse is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
           IF (NOT `the abuser was a child`)
              THEN `Rules s 6 does not take it out: the abuser was not a child; whether it is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
           IF `the abuse involved physical contact or penetration`
              THEN `Rules s 6 does not take it out: the abuse involved physical contact or penetration; whether it is within the scope is decided by Act s 14`
           OTHERWISE `out of the scope: sexual abuse by another child that involved neither physical contact with me nor penetration of me is not within the scope of the scheme (Rules s 6)`

§§ `Which institutions are responsible (Rules Part 3)`

-- Rules s 11(1): "(a) a court makes an order (except a consent order) that an institution (the defendant institution) pay
-- compensation or damages for abuse of a person to the person or a group that includes the person; and (b) the order is
-- not set aside on appeal; and (c) if the order is that the defendant institution pay the group--the person does not
-- choose not to accept the person's share of the payment to the group."
GIVEN `ordered` IS A BOOLEAN, `consent order` IS A BOOLEAN, `set aside` IS A BOOLEAN, `to a group` IS A BOOLEAN, `I chose not to take my share` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 11(1) -- a court order for compensation or damages applies` `ordered` `consent order` `set aside` `to a group` `I chose not to take my share` IF
        `ordered`
    AND (NOT `consent order`)
    AND (NOT `set aside`)
    AND (NOT (`to a group` AND `I chose not to take my share`))

DECLARE `Whether Rules s 8 makes the government equally responsible` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the participating government institution is equally responsible with the non-government institution that cared for me, and the non-government institution is not primarily responsible (Rules s 8(1), (6); Act s 15(5), (6))`
    `Rules s 8 does not apply: a court has ordered the government institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, so it is not responsible at all (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 1)`
    `Rules s 8 does not apply: the government institution is not a participating institution`
    `Rules s 8 does not make them equally responsible: not every circumstance in Rules s 8(2)-(5) existed; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`

-- Rules s 8(1): subsections (2)-(5) "together prescribe the circumstances in which a participating government institution is
-- equally responsible with a non-government institution". (2) the arrangement for day-to-day care; (3) at the time of the
-- abuse, parental responsibility under a court order, or the child a ward of the government's jurisdiction; (4) while the
-- arrangement had effect, the only persons or institutions with parental responsibility were those listed; (5) the abuse
-- occurred while the child was in the care of the non-government institution and not another institution. (6): the
-- non-government institution "is not primarily responsible". s 11(4) item 1: if the defendant institution is "a
-- participating government institution for which the conditions in subsections 8(2), (3) and (4) are met", s 8 does not
-- apply.
@export Is the government department that placed me in the care of a church, charity or other non-government institution equally responsible for the abuse with that institution (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 8)? A participating government institution is equally responsible if it arranged for the non-government institution to have my day-to-day care, it had parental responsibility for me under a court order or I was a ward of its State or Territory at the time, only the listed people or bodies had parental responsibility while the arrangement lasted, and the abuse happened while I was in that institution's care. Equal responsibility matters because each responsible participating institution shares the cost of redress and owes a direct personal response.
GIVEN `the government institution is a participating institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government department or agency is a participating institution in the scheme
      `it arranged my day-to-day care with the non-government institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government institution made an arrangement with the non-government institution (for example a church home or charity) for it to have responsibility for your day-to-day care
      `it had parental responsibility for me under a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the abuse, the government institution had parental responsibility for you under a court order (whether or not someone else also had it)
      `I was a ward of its State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the abuse, you were a ward of the State, Territory or Commonwealth that the government institution belongs to
      `only those listed had parental responsibility for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while the arrangement had effect, the only people or bodies with parental responsibility for you were the non-government institution, a person with it under a court order, the government institution, its State, Territory or Commonwealth, or (for a Territory arrangement spanning self-government) the Territory or a Territory institution
      `the abuse happened in that institution's care alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were in the care of the non-government institution and not in the care of another institution
      `a court ordered the government institution to pay me for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court ordered the government institution to pay you (or a group including you) compensation or damages for the abuse, not by consent, not set aside on appeal, and you did not refuse your share of a group payment
GIVETH A `Whether Rules s 8 makes the government equally responsible`
`Is the government that placed me equally responsible question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the government institution is a participating institution`)
              THEN `Rules s 8 does not apply: the government institution is not a participating institution`
           IF `a court ordered the government institution to pay me for the abuse` AND `s 8(2)-(4) are met`
              THEN `Rules s 8 does not apply: a court has ordered the government institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, so it is not responsible at all (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 1)`
           IF `s 8(2)-(4) are met` AND `the abuse happened in that institution's care alone`
              THEN `yes: the participating government institution is equally responsible with the non-government institution that cared for me, and the non-government institution is not primarily responsible (Rules s 8(1), (6); Act s 15(5), (6))`
           OTHERWISE `Rules s 8 does not make them equally responsible: not every circumstance in Rules s 8(2)-(5) existed; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
    WHERE
        `s 8(2)-(4) are met` MEANS
                `it arranged my day-to-day care with the non-government institution`
            AND (`it had parental responsibility for me under a court order` OR `I was a ward of its State or Territory`)
            AND `only those listed had parental responsibility for me`

DECLARE `Whether Rules s 9 makes Defence equally responsible` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a Commonwealth institution that deals with defence is equally responsible with each institution otherwise responsible for the abuse, and none of them is primarily responsible (Rules s 9(2), (3))`
    `Rules s 9 does not apply: the abuse occurred before 1 January 1977 (Rules s 9(1)(a))`
    `Rules s 9 does not apply: the conditions in Rules s 9(1)(b)-(d) are not all met; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
    `Rules s 9 does not apply: a court has ordered the Commonwealth defence institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, so it is not responsible at all (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 2)`

-- Rules s 9(1): "this section applies to abuse of a person if: (a) the abuse occurred on or after 1 January 1977; and (b)
-- the abuse was connected with the person's membership of a unit of a cadet force provided for by Commonwealth
-- legislation; and (c) the unit was associated with an institution (except a Commonwealth institution that deals with
-- defence); and (d) apart from this section, either: (i) an institution (except a Commonwealth institution that deals with
-- defence) would be primarily responsible for the abuse; or (ii) 2 or more institutions (none of them a Commonwealth
-- institution that deals with defence) would be equally responsible for the abuse." (2): those institutions and "a
-- Commonwealth institution that deals with defence" are equally responsible. (3): none is primarily responsible.
-- s 11(4) item 2: if the defendant institution is "an institution described in paragraph 9(2)(b)", s 9 does not apply.
@export Is the Department of Defence equally responsible for abuse I suffered as a cadet (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 9)? For abuse on or after 1 January 1977 connected with membership of a cadet unit set up under Commonwealth law and associated with a school or other non-defence institution, a Commonwealth defence institution is equally responsible with the institution (or institutions) that would otherwise be responsible.
GIVEN `the day the abuse occurred` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse occurred (if it happened over a period, the day of the abuse you are asking about)
      `it was connected with my membership of a cadet unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse was connected with your membership of a unit of a cadet force provided for by Commonwealth legislation (for example Army, Navy or Air Force cadets)
      `the unit was associated with a non-defence institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cadet unit was associated with an institution other than a Commonwealth defence institution (for example a school)
      `a non-defence institution would otherwise be responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, leaving this rule aside, one non-defence institution would be primarily responsible for the abuse, or two or more non-defence institutions would be equally responsible (the Operator's finding)
      `a court ordered Defence to pay me for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court ordered a Commonwealth defence institution to pay you (or a group including you) compensation or damages for the abuse, not by consent, not set aside on appeal, and you did not refuse your share of a group payment
GIVETH A `Whether Rules s 9 makes Defence equally responsible`
`Is Defence equally responsible for abuse in cadets question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a court ordered Defence to pay me for the abuse`
              THEN `Rules s 9 does not apply: a court has ordered the Commonwealth defence institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, so it is not responsible at all (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 2)`
           IF `the date` `the day the abuse occurred` `falls before` (`the calendar day` 1 1 1977)
              THEN `Rules s 9 does not apply: the abuse occurred before 1 January 1977 (Rules s 9(1)(a))`
           IF `it was connected with my membership of a cadet unit` AND `the unit was associated with a non-defence institution` AND `a non-defence institution would otherwise be responsible`
              THEN `yes: a Commonwealth institution that deals with defence is equally responsible with each institution otherwise responsible for the abuse, and none of them is primarily responsible (Rules s 9(2), (3))`
           OTHERWISE `Rules s 9 does not apply: the conditions in Rules s 9(1)(b)-(d) are not all met; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`

DECLARE `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant` IS ONE OF
    `all equally responsible: the Commonwealth Department administering the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946, the State or Territory institution that had me as its ward, and each other institution otherwise responsible (Rules s 10(2)); no institution is responsible except under s 10(2) (s 10(3))`
    `the same, except the institution a court ordered to pay me: it is not responsible, and Rules s 10 does not apply (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 3); responsibility is decided under Act s 15 and Rules s 11`
    `Rules s 10 does not apply: I am not a child migrant covered by Rules s 10(1); responsibility is decided under Act s 15`

-- Rules s 10(1): the four conditions shared with s 4B(2) (above). (2): "The following institutions are all equally
-- responsible for the abuse of the person ...: (a) the Department administered by the Minister administering section 6 of
-- the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946; (b) the State institution or Territory institution that, when the
-- abuse occurred, had responsibility for the person as a ward ...; (c) each institution that: (i) would have been
-- responsible for the abuse apart from this section; and (ii) is not covered by paragraph (a) or (b)." (3): "If, apart
-- from this section, an institution would be responsible for the abuse, the institution is not primarily responsible or
-- equally responsible for the abuse, except under subsection (2)." s 11(4) item 3: if the defendant institution is "an
-- institution described in paragraph 10(2)(a) or (b)", s 10 does not apply.
@export Who is responsible for abuse I suffered as a former child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 10)? For a child migrant who arrived before 1984 without adult family and was abused while a ward of a participating State or Territory, the Commonwealth immigration department, the State or Territory guardian and every other institution otherwise responsible are all equally responsible, with special rules that cap the Commonwealth's share.
GIVEN `the year I arrived in Australia` IS A NUMBER @desc The year you arrived in Australia, for example 1952
      `I was a child when I arrived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when you arrived in Australia
      `I was sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent to Australia from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution
      `I had no family in Australia except children when I arrived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you arrived, no members of your family were in Australia other than one or more children
      `I was sent under an Empire Settlement Act scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent under a scheme carried out under the Empire Settlement Act 1922 (United Kingdom)
      `I became a ward under the overseas children or guardianship laws` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946
      `I became a ward of a participating State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became a ward of a State or Territory that participates in the scheme
      `the abuse occurred while I was that ward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while you were a ward of that State or Territory
      `a court ordered the Department or my guardian State to pay me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court ordered the Commonwealth immigration department, or the State or Territory institution that was your guardian, to pay you (or a group including you) compensation or damages for the abuse, not by consent, not set aside on appeal, and you did not refuse your share of a group payment
GIVETH A `Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant`
`Who is responsible for abuse of a child migrant question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`Rules s 4B(2)(a) -- I arrived before 1984 as an unaccompanied child migrant` `the year I arrived in Australia` `I was a child when I arrived` `I was sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution` `I had no family in Australia except children when I arrived` AND (`I was sent under an Empire Settlement Act scheme` OR `I became a ward under the overseas children or guardianship laws`) AND `I became a ward of a participating State or Territory` AND `the abuse occurred while I was that ward`))
              THEN `Rules s 10 does not apply: I am not a child migrant covered by Rules s 10(1); responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
           IF `a court ordered the Department or my guardian State to pay me`
              THEN `the same, except the institution a court ordered to pay me: it is not responsible, and Rules s 10 does not apply (Rules s 11(2), (4) item 3); responsibility is decided under Act s 15 and Rules s 11`
           OTHERWISE `all equally responsible: the Commonwealth Department administering the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946, the State or Territory institution that had me as its ward, and each other institution otherwise responsible (Rules s 10(2)); no institution is responsible except under s 10(2) (s 10(3))`

DECLARE `Whether an institution ordered by a court to pay me is responsible` IS ONE OF
    `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); and no other institution is responsible for it either (s 11(3))`
    `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); other institutions may still be responsible`
    `Rules s 11 does not apply: no court has ordered the institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse`
    `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was a consent order (Rules s 11(1)(a))`
    `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was set aside on appeal (Rules s 11(1)(b))`
    `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was for a group payment and I chose not to accept my share (Rules s 11(1)(c))`

-- Rules s 11(2): "The defendant institution is not responsible, primarily responsible or equally responsible for the
-- abuse." (3): "If: (a) the defendant institution and one or more other institutions are approximately equally responsible
-- for the abuser having contact with the person; and (b) apart from subsection (2) the defendant institution would have
-- been primarily responsible for the abuse; none of the other institutions is equally responsible (or primarily
-- responsible or responsible) for the abuse." (See NOTES.md, finding 4, on how (a) and (b) sit together.)
@export If a court has ordered an institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse, is that institution still responsible under the redress scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 11)? A court order (not a consent order) that is not set aside on appeal takes that institution out of the scheme for that abuse, so it does not pay redress for it. A settlement you agreed to is not a court order of this kind.
GIVEN `a court ordered the institution to pay me or my group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court has ordered the institution to pay compensation or damages for the abuse to you, or to a group (such as a class action group) that includes you
      `it was a consent order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order was a consent order (made by agreement between the parties)
      `it was set aside on appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order has been set aside on appeal
      `the order was to pay a group` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the order was for payment to a group that includes you, rather than to you alone
      `I chose not to accept my share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you chose not to accept your share of the payment to the group
      `the institutions were about equally responsible for the abuser's contact with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the institution and one or more other institutions were approximately equally responsible for the abuser having contact with you (the Operator's finding)
      `the institution would otherwise have been primarily responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, leaving the court order aside, the institution would have been primarily responsible for the abuse (the Operator's finding)
GIVETH A `Whether an institution ordered by a court to pay me is responsible`
`Is an institution ordered by a court to pay me still responsible question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `a court ordered the institution to pay me or my group`)
              THEN `Rules s 11 does not apply: no court has ordered the institution to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse`
           IF `it was a consent order`
              THEN `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was a consent order (Rules s 11(1)(a))`
           IF `it was set aside on appeal`
              THEN `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was set aside on appeal (Rules s 11(1)(b))`
           IF `the order was to pay a group` AND `I chose not to accept my share`
              THEN `Rules s 11 does not apply: the order was for a group payment and I chose not to accept my share (Rules s 11(1)(c))`
           IF `the institutions were about equally responsible for the abuser's contact with me` AND `the institution would otherwise have been primarily responsible`
              THEN `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); and no other institution is responsible for it either (s 11(3))`
           OTHERWISE `not responsible: the institution ordered to pay me is not responsible for the abuse under the scheme (Rules s 11(2)); other institutions may still be responsible`

DECLARE `Whether a government authority is responsible` IS ONE OF
    `not responsible: the government authority's only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12(2))`
    `Rules s 12 gives way: the authority is responsible under Rules Part 3 Division 2 (ss 8-10), which s 12 is subject to (s 12(3))`
    `Rules s 12 does not apply: the institution is not an authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
    `Rules s 12 does not apply: the abuse was not in another institution's care, by its official, or on its premises or in its activities (Rules s 12(1))`
    `Rules s 12 does not apply: the authority had some other connection with the abuse; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`

-- Rules s 12(1): an authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory, for abuse that "(a) occurred while another
-- institution was responsible for the day-to-day care or custody of the person or was the legal guardian of the person; or
-- (b) was carried out by a person who was an official of another institution ...; or (c) occurred: (i) on the premises of
-- another institution; or (ii) where activities of another institution took place; or (iii) in connection with the
-- activities of another institution." (2): "the only connection between the government authority and the abuse is one or
-- more of the following: (a) ... regulated the other institution or an activity ...; (b) ... funded the other institution
-- or an activity ...; (c) the other institution was established by or under the law of the jurisdiction that the
-- government authority belongs to." (3): "This section has effect subject to Division 2."
@export Is a government body responsible for abuse at a school, club, church or other institution only because it regulated, funded or set up that institution (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 12)? A Commonwealth, State or Territory authority whose only link to the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the institution where the abuse happened is not responsible, unless the special rules for government placements, cadets or child migrants make it equally responsible.
GIVEN `the institution is a Commonwealth, State or Territory authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the body you are asking about is an authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory (such as a government department)
      `the abuse was in or by another institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse happened while another institution had your day-to-day care, custody or guardianship, or was by an official of another institution, or happened on another institution's premises, where its activities took place or in connection with its activities
      `the authority regulated the other institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government authority regulated the other institution or one of its activities
      `the authority funded the other institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government authority funded the other institution or one of its activities
      `the other institution was set up under the authority's law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other institution was established by or under a law of the authority's own jurisdiction
      `the authority had some other connection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the government authority had any other connection with the abuse (for example, it placed you there, was your guardian, or employed the abuser)
      `the authority is responsible under Rules ss 8 to 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the authority is equally responsible under the rules for government placements, cadets or child migrants (Rules ss 8, 9 or 10)
GIVETH A `Whether a government authority is responsible`
`Is a government body that only regulated or funded responsible question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the institution is a Commonwealth, State or Territory authority`)
              THEN `Rules s 12 does not apply: the institution is not an authority of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory`
           IF `the authority is responsible under Rules ss 8 to 10`
              THEN `Rules s 12 gives way: the authority is responsible under Rules Part 3 Division 2 (ss 8-10), which s 12 is subject to (s 12(3))`
           IF (NOT `the abuse was in or by another institution`)
              THEN `Rules s 12 does not apply: the abuse was not in another institution's care, by its official, or on its premises or in its activities (Rules s 12(1))`
           IF `the authority had some other connection` OR (NOT (`the authority regulated the other institution` OR `the authority funded the other institution` OR `the other institution was set up under the authority's law`))
              THEN `Rules s 12 does not apply: the authority had some other connection with the abuse; responsibility is decided under Act s 15`
           OTHERWISE `not responsible: the government authority's only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12(2))`

§§ `If I applied as a child (Rules Part 4)`

DECLARE `My timetable as a child applicant` IS ONE OF
    `the Operator must give me a notice in this window, and cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day; then it must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` HAS
        `the window opens` IS A DATE
        `the window closes` IS A DATE
        `I turn 18 on` IS A DATE
    `no notice is required because I applied less than 4 months before turning 18; the Operator cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day, then must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` HAS
        `I turn 18 on` IS A DATE
    `Rules s 15 does not apply: I was not a child on the day I applied`
    `Rules s 15 does not apply: I will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (1 July 2028); Act s 20(1)(c) bars the application`

GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE, `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 15(2) -- I applied at least 4 months before turning 18` `the day I applied` `my date of birth` IF
    `the date` `the day I applied` `falls on or before` (`the matching day` (0 MINUS 4) `months from` (`the eighteenth birthday for` `my date of birth`))

-- Rules s 15(1): "This section has effect for the purposes of section 21 of the Act if an application for redress is made
-- by a person who is a child who will turn 18 before the scheme sunset day." (2): "If the application is made at least 4
-- months before the day the person turns 18, the Operator must give the person a notice at least 3 months, but not more
-- than 6 months, before that day: (a) informing the person that a determination ... will be made as soon as practicable
-- after the person turns 18; and (b) inviting the person to give the Operator, before the person turns 18, any further
-- information ..." (3): "The Operator must not make a determination ... before the person turns 18." (4): "... must make a
-- determination ... as soon as practicable after the person turns 18 ..."
@export I applied for redress as a child: when will the Operator write to me, and when will my application be decided (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 15)? The Operator cannot decide a child's application before the child turns 18, and must decide it as soon as practicable afterwards. If you applied at least 4 months before turning 18, the Operator must write to you between 6 and 3 months before your 18th birthday, telling you this and inviting you to send any further information before you turn 18.
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your application for redress
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
GIVETH A `My timetable as a child applicant`
`When will my application as a child be decided question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the date` `the day I applied` `falls on or after` `I turn 18`
              THEN `Rules s 15 does not apply: I was not a child on the day I applied`
           IF `the date` `I turn 18` `falls on or after` `the sunset day of the scheme`
              THEN `Rules s 15 does not apply: I will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (1 July 2028); Act s 20(1)(c) bars the application`
           IF `Rules s 15(2) -- I applied at least 4 months before turning 18` `the day I applied` `my date of birth`
              THEN `the Operator must give me a notice in this window, and cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day; then it must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` (`the matching day` (0 MINUS 6) `months from` `I turn 18`) (`the matching day` (0 MINUS 3) `months from` `I turn 18`) `I turn 18`
           OTHERWISE `no notice is required because I applied less than 4 months before turning 18; the Operator cannot decide before I turn 18 on this day, then must decide as soon as practicable (Rules s 15(2)-(4))` `I turn 18`
    WHERE
        `I turn 18` MEANS `the eighteenth birthday for` `my date of birth`

-- Rules s 15(2) as a regulative rule, counted in days from the day of the application (day 0): the Operator must give the
-- notice no later than the last day of the window; a notice before the window opens does not count (PROVIDED).
GIVEN `the opening day` IS A NUMBER, `the closing day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Rules party` `Rules step`
`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` `the opening day` `the closing day` MEANS
    PARTY `the Operator`
    MUST `give me the notice about turning 18` `the notice day` PROVIDED `the notice day` AT LEAST `the opening day`
    WITHIN `the closing day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Operator` BECAUSE "no notice between 6 months and 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); the Operator still must not decide before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(3))"

GIVEN `the opening day` IS A NUMBER, `the closing day` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 15(2) -- a notice on this day meets the rule` `the opening day` `the closing day` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me a notice 3 to 6 months before I turn 18` `the opening day` `the closing day`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice about turning 18` `the day`) `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my notice about turning 18 stands` IS ONE OF
    `no notice is required (Rules s 15(2) does not apply to my application)`
    `given in time (Rules s 15(2))`
    `given too early: more than 6 months before I turn 18, so it is not the notice Rules s 15(2) requires; that notice is still owed`
    `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
    `late: the Operator did not give me the notice by 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); it still must not decide before I turn 18 (s 15(3))`

@export I applied for redress as a child: has the Operator given me, in time, the notice it must give me before I turn 18 (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 15(2))? If you applied at least 4 months before your 18th birthday, the notice must come no earlier than 6 months and no later than 3 months before that birthday.
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your application for redress
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `I have been given the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has given you the notice saying your application will be decided after you turn 18 and inviting further information
      `the day I was given the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the Operator gave you that notice (any date if you have not been given it)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my notice about turning 18 stands`
`Has the Operator given me my notice about turning 18 in time question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the date` `the day I applied` `falls before` `I turn 18` AND `the date` `I turn 18` `falls before` `the sunset day of the scheme` AND `Rules s 15(2) -- I applied at least 4 months before turning 18` `the day I applied` `my date of birth`))
              THEN `no notice is required (Rules s 15(2) does not apply to my application)`
           IF `I have been given the notice` AND `the date` `the day I was given the notice` `falls before` `the first notice day`
              THEN `given too early: more than 6 months before I turn 18, so it is not the notice Rules s 15(2) requires; that notice is still owed`
           IF `I have been given the notice` AND `Rules s 15(2) -- a notice on this day meets the rule` `the opening day number` `the closing day number` (`the days from` `the day I applied` `until` `the day I was given the notice`)
              THEN `given in time (Rules s 15(2))`
           IF `I have been given the notice`
              THEN `late: the Operator did not give me the notice by 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); it still must not decide before I turn 18 (s 15(3))`
           IF `the date` `today` `falls on or before` `the last notice day`
              THEN `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
           OTHERWISE `late: the Operator did not give me the notice by 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); it still must not decide before I turn 18 (s 15(3))`
    WHERE
        `I turn 18` MEANS `the eighteenth birthday for` `my date of birth`
        `the first notice day` MEANS `the matching day` (0 MINUS 6) `months from` `I turn 18`
        `the last notice day` MEANS `the matching day` (0 MINUS 3) `months from` `I turn 18`
        `the opening day number` MEANS `the days from` `the day I applied` `until` `the first notice day`
        `the closing day number` MEANS `the days from` `the day I applied` `until` `the last notice day`

§§ `Can the decision on my application be revoked (Rules Part 5)`

DECLARE `Whether my determination can be revoked` IS ONE OF
    `cannot be revoked: I have accepted the offer of redress (Act s 29(5))`
    `must be revoked: I notified the Operator that I accepted an offer of payment relating to the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(a), s 74)`
    `must be revoked: the Operator has learned for the first time of a payment to me under a court order for the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(b), (4)(a))`
    `must be revoked: the Operator has learned for the first time of a payment to me by or for a responsible institution for the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(b), (4)(b))`
    `may be revoked: the Operator has received information it did not have that would have changed the determination (Rules s 17(2))`
    `Rules s 17 gives the Operator no ground to revoke on these facts`

-- Rules s 17(2): "The Operator may revoke the determination if, after the Operator made the determination, the Operator
-- receives information that: (a) the Operator did not have before making the determination; and (b) is such that, had the
-- Operator had the information ..., the Operator would not have made the determination or would have made a different
-- determination." (3): "However, the Operator must revoke the determination if ... the Operator: (a) receives notification
-- from the person under section 74 ...; or (b) is informed (for the first time) that a payment covered by subsection (4)
-- was paid to the person before or after the determination was made." (4): "(a) a payment paid to the person under an
-- order described in paragraphs 11(1)(a) and (b); (b) a payment paid to the person by, or on behalf of, a responsible
-- institution in relation to abuse for which the institution is responsible, except to the extent that the payment is
-- covered by any of subsections 26(3), (4) and (5)." Act s 29(5): no revocation of an approval once the offer is accepted.
-- What follows a revocation (Act s 29(6), (7)): the determination is taken never to have been made, an open offer is
-- withdrawn, a review application is withdrawn, and I must be given written notice.
@export Can the Operator revoke its decision on my redress application (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 17)? The Operator must revoke it if you tell it you have accepted a payment offer from a responsible institution, or it learns for the first time of a court-ordered payment or an institution's payment to you for the abuse (other than payments the Rules exclude). It may revoke it if new information would have changed the decision. It cannot revoke an approval once you have accepted the offer of redress. If revoked, the decision is treated as never made, any open offer and any review application are withdrawn, and you must be told in writing.
GIVEN `I have accepted the offer of redress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already accepted your offer of redress
      `I told the Operator I accepted a payment offer from a responsible institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the decision, you notified the Operator (under Rules s 74) that you had accepted an offer of a payment from a responsible institution relating to the abuse
      `the Operator first learned of a court-ordered payment to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the decision, the Operator was told for the first time that you were paid under a court order (not a consent order, not set aside on appeal) for compensation or damages for the abuse
      `the Operator first learned of an institution's payment to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the decision, the Operator was told for the first time that a responsible institution (or someone on its behalf) paid you in relation to the abuse
      `all of that payment is excluded by Rules s 26(3) to (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the whole of that institution's payment is one the Rules exclude (workers' or veterans' compensation under the listed Acts, amounts not for the abuse or harm, amounts for expenses, or payments for non-sexual abuse alone)
      `the Operator received new information that would have changed the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, after the decision, the Operator received information it did not have before and that would have led it not to make, or to make a different, decision (the Operator's view)
GIVETH A `Whether my determination can be revoked`
`Can the decision on my application be revoked question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I have accepted the offer of redress`
              THEN `cannot be revoked: I have accepted the offer of redress (Act s 29(5))`
           IF `I told the Operator I accepted a payment offer from a responsible institution`
              THEN `must be revoked: I notified the Operator that I accepted an offer of payment relating to the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(a), s 74)`
           IF `the Operator first learned of a court-ordered payment to me`
              THEN `must be revoked: the Operator has learned for the first time of a payment to me under a court order for the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(b), (4)(a))`
           IF `the Operator first learned of an institution's payment to me` AND (NOT `all of that payment is excluded by Rules s 26(3) to (5)`)
              THEN `must be revoked: the Operator has learned for the first time of a payment to me by or for a responsible institution for the abuse (Rules s 17(3)(b), (4)(b))`
           IF `the Operator received new information that would have changed the decision`
              THEN `may be revoked: the Operator has received information it did not have that would have changed the determination (Rules s 17(2))`
           OTHERWISE `Rules s 17 gives the Operator no ground to revoke on these facts`

§§ `Earlier payments for the abuse (Rules Part 6 Division 3)`

DECLARE `The kind of earlier payment` IS ONE OF
    `compensation under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988`
    `a payment under Part II, III or XI of the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation (Defence-related Claims) Act 1988`
    `a payment under Chapter 3, 4, 5, 5A, 6 or 11 of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004`
    `a payment under a Part of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986 listed in Rules s 26(3)(d)`
    `a payment under Part 2, 3 or 3A of the Australian Participants in British Nuclear Tests and British Commonwealth Occupation Force (Treatment) Act 2006`
    `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)`

-- Act s 30(2) step 3: a relevant prior payment is "any payment ... paid to the person by, or on behalf of, the responsible
-- institution in relation to abuse for which the institution is responsible (but do not include any payment to the extent
-- that it is prescribed by the rules as not being a relevant prior payment)". Rules s 26(3): the listed payments are "not a
-- relevant prior payment (to any extent)". (4): "not a relevant prior payment to the extent that: (a) it is not in
-- recognition of: (i) the abuse; or (ii) harm caused by the abuse; or (b) it is reasonably attributable to: (i) expenses of
-- medical, dental or other treatment; or (ii) any other expenses." (5): a payment for non-sexual abuse "is not a relevant
-- prior payment (to any extent) if the non-sexual abuse is not covered by a set of abuse that also covers sexual abuse".
-- (6): a payment made by or for several responsible institutions counts only to an extent worked out by a formula that
-- the deposit lost (NOTES.md, finding 1): NOTHING.
@export How much of an earlier payment I received from an institution for the abuse will count against my redress payment (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 26)? Payments from an institution responsible for the abuse are deducted (indexed) from that institution's share of your redress payment, but not workers' compensation or veterans' and military compensation under the listed Acts, not the parts that were not for the abuse or the harm it caused, not the parts for medical, dental, treatment, living or other expenses, and not payments for non-sexual abuse alone. Answers in Australian dollars; no answer where the payment was made for several institutions together.
GIVEN `it was paid by or for an institution responsible for the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was paid to you by, or on behalf of, an institution responsible for the abuse, in relation to that abuse
      `the kind of payment` IS A `The kind of earlier payment` @desc What the payment was: compensation under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988; a payment under Part II, III or XI of the Defence-related Claims Act 1988; a payment under Chapter 3, 4, 5, 5A, 6 or 11 of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004; a payment under a listed Part of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; a payment under Part 2, 3 or 3A of the British Nuclear Tests Treatment Act 2006; or any other payment
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you were paid, in Australian dollars
      `the part not for the abuse or its harm` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the payment was not in recognition of the abuse or of harm caused by it, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `the part for treatment or other expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of the payment is reasonably attributable to medical, dental or other treatment, living expenses or other expenses, in Australian dollars, not counting again anything in the previous answer (0 if none)
      `it was for non-sexual abuse alone` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was for non-sexual abuse that is not covered by a set of abuse that also covers sexual abuse of you
      `it was paid by or for more than one responsible institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was made by one responsible institution on behalf of others responsible for the abuse, or on its behalf by another responsible institution
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it was paid by or for an institution responsible for the abuse`)
              THEN JUST 0
           IF (NOT (`the kind of payment` EQUALS `any other payment (for example a settlement, an ex gratia payment or a payment under an institution's own scheme)`))
              THEN JUST 0
           IF `it was for non-sexual abuse alone`
              THEN JUST 0
           IF `it was paid by or for more than one responsible institution`
              THEN NOTHING
           IF `the counted part` LESS THAN 0
              THEN JUST 0
           OTHERWISE JUST `the counted part`
    WHERE
        `the counted part` MEANS `the amount paid` MINUS (`the part not for the abuse or its harm` PLUS `the part for treatment or other expenses`)

§§ `Accepting my offer (Rules Part 7)`

DECLARE `Whether my acceptance document has what the Rules require` IS ONE OF
    `complete: it has each responsible institution's share of the costs, the earlier payments and their effect, and my consent for released institutions and officials (Rules s 31)`
    `missing: the amount of each responsible institution's share of the costs of the redress payment (Rules s 31(2)(a))`
    `missing: the amount of an earlier payment from a responsible institution, or a statement of its effect on that institution's share (Rules s 31(2)(b))`
    `missing: my consent to released institutions and officials using and disclosing my protected information in the document to obtain the benefit of Act s 43 (Rules s 31(3))`

-- Rules s 31(2): "The document must include, for each responsible institution that is responsible for any of the abuse:
-- (a) the amount of the institution's share of the costs of the redress payment; and (b) if a relevant prior payment has
-- been paid to the person by, or on behalf of, the institution: (i) the amount of that payment; and (ii) a statement of the
-- effect of the payment on the amount of the institution's share ..." (3): "The document must also include the person's
-- consent to each released institution or official identified in the document using and disclosing protected information
-- about the person, that is included in the document, for the purpose of the institution or official obtaining the
-- benefit of section 43 of the Act ..." (s 43: the release from civil liability once I accept.)
@export Does the acceptance document for my offer of redress contain what the Rules require (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 31)? It must show each responsible institution's share of the cost of your redress payment, any earlier payment from that institution and how it changed that share, and your consent for each institution or official you release to use and disclose your information in the document so it can rely on the release from civil claims that acceptance brings.
GIVEN `it states each institution's share of the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document states, for each responsible institution, the amount of its share of the costs of your redress payment
      `an institution made an earlier payment to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any responsible institution (or someone on its behalf) made an earlier payment to you that counts against your redress payment
      `it states each earlier payment and its effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document states the amount of each such earlier payment and how it changed that institution's share
      `it includes my consent for released institutions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the document includes your consent to each released institution or official named in it using and disclosing your information in the document to rely on the release from civil liability
GIVETH A `Whether my acceptance document has what the Rules require`
`Does my acceptance document have what the Rules require question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `it states each institution's share of the costs`)
              THEN `missing: the amount of each responsible institution's share of the costs of the redress payment (Rules s 31(2)(a))`
           IF `an institution made an earlier payment to me` AND (NOT `it states each earlier payment and its effect`)
              THEN `missing: the amount of an earlier payment from a responsible institution, or a statement of its effect on that institution's share (Rules s 31(2)(b))`
           IF (NOT `it includes my consent for released institutions`)
              THEN `missing: my consent to released institutions and officials using and disclosing my protected information in the document to obtain the benefit of Act s 43 (Rules s 31(3))`
           OTHERWISE `complete: it has each responsible institution's share of the costs, the earlier payments and their effect, and my consent for released institutions and officials (Rules s 31)`

§§ `Being paid (Rules Part 8 Division 2)`

DECLARE `Where my redress payment goes` IS ONE OF
    `into an account I hold with a financial institution and have nominated in writing to the Operator (Rules s 33(2))`
    `into an account with a financial institution nominated in writing by the executor or administrator of my estate (Rules s 33(3))`
    `into an account the administrator appointed for my affairs holds with a financial institution and has nominated in writing (Rules s 33(4); Act s 48(1A))`
    `already paid into my nominated account; Rules s 33 asks for nothing more`

-- Rules s 33(2): "Subject to subsections (3) and (4), a redress payment, or a counselling and psychological services
-- payment, for a person must be paid to an account that: (a) the person holds with a financial institution; and (b) the
-- person has nominated in writing to the Operator." (3): "Despite subsection (2), ... must be paid to an account ...
-- nominated in writing to the Operator by the executor or administrator of the person's estate if: (a) the person has died
-- after becoming entitled to redress under the scheme; and (b) the payment has not been made in accordance with that
-- subsection; and (c) it is no longer possible to make the payment in accordance with that subsection." (4): "Despite
-- subsection (2), where subsection 48(1A) of the Act applies, ... must be paid to an account that: (a) is held by the
-- administrator ...; and (b) the administrator has nominated in writing to the Operator." Fork F5: where both (3) and (4)
-- could apply, (3) is taken.
@export Into which bank account will my redress payment (or counselling payment) be paid (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 33)? Normally into an account you hold and have nominated in writing. If a court or tribunal has appointed an administrator for your financial affairs and the Operator pays the administrator, into the administrator's nominated account. If you die after becoming entitled and the payment can no longer be made into your account, into an account nominated by your executor or administrator.
GIVEN `an administrator for my affairs is to be paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court, tribunal or board has appointed an administrator to make decisions about your property or financial affairs, and the Operator considers it appropriate to pay the administrator (not someone holding your power of attorney)
      `I have died after becoming entitled to redress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person entitled to redress has died after becoming entitled (answer for the person who was entitled)
      `the payment has been made into my nominated account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment has already been made into the account nominated by the person entitled
      `it can no longer be paid into my nominated account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is no longer possible to pay into that account (for example, it was closed after the death)
GIVETH A `Where my redress payment goes`
`Where will my redress payment be paid question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the payment has been made into my nominated account`
              THEN `already paid into my nominated account; Rules s 33 asks for nothing more`
           IF `I have died after becoming entitled to redress` AND `it can no longer be paid into my nominated account`
              THEN `into an account with a financial institution nominated in writing by the executor or administrator of my estate (Rules s 33(3))`
           IF `an administrator for my affairs is to be paid`
              THEN `into an account the administrator appointed for my affairs holds with a financial institution and has nominated in writing (Rules s 33(4); Act s 48(1A))`
           OTHERWISE `into an account I hold with a financial institution and have nominated in writing to the Operator (Rules s 33(2))`

§§ `If the applicant dies (Rules Part 8 Division 3) [only if an applicant has died]`

DECLARE `When the applicant died` IS ONE OF
    `before the Operator decided the application (Act s 58)`
    `after an offer of redress, before it was accepted, declined or withdrawn, with no review pending (Act s 59(3))`
    `after an offer of redress, while a review of the decision was pending (Act s 59(4))`
    `during a reassessment, after applying for review of the reassessment decision (Act s 71M(4))`
    `during a reassessment, before the reassessment decision (Act s 71N(3))`
    `before the current determination was identified for reassessment (Act s 71P(3))`
    `after accepting the offer of redress`

DECLARE `The notice when the applicant dies` IS ONE OF
    `a written notice to the person the Operator considers most appropriate (not an institution): whether the application was approved, the reasons, and if approved the amount of the redress payment (Rules s 34)`
    `a written notice to each person the Operator decides should be paid the redress payment, stating the amount to be paid to that person (Rules s 35(2); Act s 60)`
    `a written notice of the outcome of the review to the person or persons the Operator considers most appropriate: the outcome (including whether the payment is payable under Act s 60 and to whom) and the reasons (Rules s 35(3), (4))`
    `a written notice of the reassessment decision to the person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons for the review of the reassessment decision, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35A)`
    `a written notice of the reassessment decision to each person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35B)`
    `a written notice of the reassessment decision to the person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35C)`
    `none under Rules Part 8 Division 3: the offer was accepted, so the redress is paid under Rules s 33`

@export The person who applied for redress has died: who will the Operator write to, and what must the notice say (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) ss 34-35C)? It depends on when the applicant died: before a decision, after an offer was made, while a review was pending, or during a reassessment. The Operator writes to the person it considers most appropriate, or to the people it decides should be paid, and states the decision, the reasons and the amounts.
GIVEN `when the applicant died` IS A `When the applicant died` @desc When the applicant died: before the Operator decided the application; after an offer, before it was accepted, declined or withdrawn, with no review pending; after an offer, while a review was pending; during a reassessment after applying for review of the reassessment decision; during a reassessment before the reassessment decision; before the current determination was identified for reassessment; or after accepting the offer
GIVETH A `The notice when the applicant dies`
`What notice follows the applicant's death question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when the applicant died`
    WHEN `before the Operator decided the application (Act s 58)` THEN `a written notice to the person the Operator considers most appropriate (not an institution): whether the application was approved, the reasons, and if approved the amount of the redress payment (Rules s 34)`
    WHEN `after an offer of redress, before it was accepted, declined or withdrawn, with no review pending (Act s 59(3))` THEN `a written notice to each person the Operator decides should be paid the redress payment, stating the amount to be paid to that person (Rules s 35(2); Act s 60)`
    WHEN `after an offer of redress, while a review of the decision was pending (Act s 59(4))` THEN `a written notice of the outcome of the review to the person or persons the Operator considers most appropriate: the outcome (including whether the payment is payable under Act s 60 and to whom) and the reasons (Rules s 35(3), (4))`
    WHEN `during a reassessment, after applying for review of the reassessment decision (Act s 71M(4))` THEN `a written notice of the reassessment decision to the person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons for the review of the reassessment decision, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35A)`
    WHEN `during a reassessment, before the reassessment decision (Act s 71N(3))` THEN `a written notice of the reassessment decision to each person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35B)`
    WHEN `before the current determination was identified for reassessment (Act s 71P(3))` THEN `a written notice of the reassessment decision to the person the Operator considers most appropriate: the reasons, the total redress payable, and any increase over the current determination (Rules s 35C)`
    WHEN `after accepting the offer of redress` THEN `none under Rules Part 8 Division 3: the offer was accepted, so the redress is paid under Rules s 33`

§§ `Notices about serious convictions and security notices (Rules Parts 9, 10) [only if I have a serious conviction or a security notice]`

DECLARE `Whether I will be told the special assessment decision` IS ONE OF
    `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision, and also each institution it asked for information about my application (Rules s 37(2))`
    `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision (Rules s 37(2)(a))`
    `Rules s 37 does not apply: the Operator has decided that I am not prevented from being entitled to redress`
    `Rules s 37 does not apply: neither a sentence for an offence in Act s 63(2)(a) nor a special assessment determination`

-- Rules s 37(1): "this section applies if the Operator: (a) becomes aware that a person who has made an application for
-- redress has been sentenced for an offence listed at paragraph 63(2)(a) of the Act, or (b) has determined under subsection
-- 63(2B) ... the person should undergo a special assessment process; and (c) decides under section 63 of the Act not to make
-- a determination that the person is not prevented from being entitled to redress ..." (2): "The Operator must give
-- written notice of the decision to: (a) the person; and (b) if, under section 25 of the Act, the Operator has requested
-- one or more participating institutions or partly-participating institutions to give the Operator information ...--each
-- of those institutions."
@export I have been sentenced to 5 years or more in prison: will I be told if the Operator decides my conviction stops me getting redress (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 37)? If you were sentenced for unlawful killing, a sexual offence, a terrorism offence or a related offence, or the Operator decided you should undergo a special assessment, and the Operator then decides not to find that you are still entitled, it must tell you in writing, and also any institution it asked for information about your application.
GIVEN `I was sentenced for an offence listed in Act s 63(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sentenced to 5 years or more for unlawful killing (or attempt or conspiracy), a sexual offence (or one including intent to commit one), or a terrorism offence (or a substantially similar State, Territory or foreign offence)
      `the Operator decided I should undergo a special assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator determined, because of exceptional circumstances, that you should undergo a special assessment process (Act s 63(2B))
      `the Operator decided not to find me still entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has decided not to make a determination that you are not prevented from being entitled to redress
      `the Operator asked institutions for information about my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator asked one or more participating or partly-participating institutions for information about your application (Act s 25)
GIVETH A `Whether I will be told the special assessment decision`
`Will I be told the special assessment decision question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`I was sentenced for an offence listed in Act s 63(2)(a)` OR `the Operator decided I should undergo a special assessment`))
              THEN `Rules s 37 does not apply: neither a sentence for an offence in Act s 63(2)(a) nor a special assessment determination`
           IF (NOT `the Operator decided not to find me still entitled`)
              THEN `Rules s 37 does not apply: the Operator has decided that I am not prevented from being entitled to redress`
           IF `the Operator asked institutions for information about my application`
              THEN `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision, and also each institution it asked for information about my application (Rules s 37(2))`
           OTHERWISE `yes: the Operator must give me written notice of its decision (Rules s 37(2)(a))`

DECLARE `Where my application stood when the security notice came into force` IS ONE OF
    `I had applied, and no decision or no offer had yet been made`
    `I had an offer of redress not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn`
    `I had agreed to a reassessment, and no reassessment decision had been made`
    `I had agreed to a reassessment, and had a new offer not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn`
    `I had already accepted or declined my offer`

DECLARE `What a security notice does to my application` IS ONE OF
    `my application is taken to be withdrawn (Act s 71(1)); the Operator must give me written notice of the withdrawal (Rules s 39(2)(a))`
    `my offer is taken to be withdrawn, the decision revoked and my application withdrawn (Act s 71(2)); the Operator must give written notice of all three to me and to each institution and person it had notified of the decision or offer, unless that institution gets notice of the withdrawal under Act s 23 (Rules s 39(2), (3))`
    `I am taken to have revoked my agreement to the reassessment (Act s 71(2A)); Rules s 39 applies, but s 39(2) names no notice of a revoked agreement`
    `my new offer is taken to be withdrawn, the reassessment decision revoked and my agreement to the reassessment revoked (Act s 71(2B)); Rules s 39(2)(b)(iii)-(iv) point to notices to those told of the reassessment, but s 39(2) names no notice of these three effects`
    `Rules s 39 does not apply: Act s 71 does not reach an offer already accepted or declined`

-- Rules s 39(1): the section applies where, because of Act s 71(1), (2), (2A) or (2B), the application is taken to be
-- withdrawn; or the application withdrawn, the determination revoked and the offer withdrawn; or the person is taken to have
-- revoked the agreement to reassessment; or the new offer withdrawn, the reassessment decision revoked and the agreement
-- revoked. (2): "The Operator must give written notice of the withdrawal of the application and, if relevant, the
-- revocation of the determination and withdrawal of the offer, to: (a) the person; and (b) if the determination is revoked
-- and the offer withdrawn--each institution and person to which the Operator was required: (i) by sections 35 and 35A of
-- the Act to give notice of the determination; or (ii) by section 41 ... of the offer; (iii) by section 71E ...; or (iv)
-- by section 71F ..." (3): no notice to an institution that Act s 23 or s 71C already requires to be told. See NOTES.md,
-- finding 6.
@export A security notice has been given about me: what happens to my redress application, and will I be told (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 39; Act s 71)? A security notice from the Home Affairs Minister withdraws a pending application, and withdraws an open offer and revokes the decision behind it; the Operator must tell you in writing, and tell the institutions it notified of the decision or offer. A pending reassessment agreement is taken to be revoked.
GIVEN `where my application stood` IS A `Where my application stood when the security notice came into force` @desc Where your application stood when the security notice came into force: applied, with no decision or no offer yet; an offer not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn; agreed to a reassessment with no reassessment decision yet; agreed to a reassessment with a new offer not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn; or the offer already accepted or declined
GIVETH A `What a security notice does to my application`
`What does a security notice do to my application question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where my application stood`
    WHEN `I had applied, and no decision or no offer had yet been made` THEN `my application is taken to be withdrawn (Act s 71(1)); the Operator must give me written notice of the withdrawal (Rules s 39(2)(a))`
    WHEN `I had an offer of redress not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn` THEN `my offer is taken to be withdrawn, the decision revoked and my application withdrawn (Act s 71(2)); the Operator must give written notice of all three to me and to each institution and person it had notified of the decision or offer, unless that institution gets notice of the withdrawal under Act s 23 (Rules s 39(2), (3))`
    WHEN `I had agreed to a reassessment, and no reassessment decision had been made` THEN `I am taken to have revoked my agreement to the reassessment (Act s 71(2A)); Rules s 39 applies, but s 39(2) names no notice of a revoked agreement`
    WHEN `I had agreed to a reassessment, and had a new offer not yet accepted, declined or withdrawn` THEN `my new offer is taken to be withdrawn, the reassessment decision revoked and my agreement to the reassessment revoked (Act s 71(2B)); Rules s 39(2)(b)(iii)-(iv) point to notices to those told of the reassessment, but s 39(2) names no notice of these three effects`
    WHEN `I had already accepted or declined my offer` THEN `Rules s 39 does not apply: Act s 71 does not reach an offer already accepted or declined`

§§ `Who may be told about me (Rules Part 11)`

DECLARE `The purpose of the disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `protecting the public revenue (Rules s 44)`
    `an offence against Commonwealth, State or Territory officers, property or the Department's premises (Rules s 45)`
    `a proceeds of crime or unexplained wealth order, disclosed to a law enforcement agency (Rules s 46)`
    `extradition (Rules s 47)`
    `international assistance in criminal matters, disclosed to the responsible Minister or Department (Rules s 48)`
    `correcting a mistake of fact that puts the scheme at risk or was published (Rules s 49)`
    `briefing a listed Minister on my complaint, a meeting or forum, or my public statements (Rules s 50)`
    `locating a missing person, disclosed to a court, coroner, Royal Commission or government authority (Rules s 51)`
    `matters about a deceased person (Rules s 52(1))`
    `establishing a death or where it is registered (Rules s 52(2))`
    `research, statistics or policy on institutional child sexual abuse (Rules s 53)`
    `contacting me about compensation in a reparation process, disclosed to a government authority (Rules s 54)`
    `aged care means testing (Rules s 54A)`
    `some other purpose`

DECLARE `The recipient of the disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `someone with a genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with that purpose`
    `a Minister listed in Rules s 43(2)`
    `someone else`

DECLARE `Whether my information can be disclosed in the public interest` IS ONE OF
    `may be certified: the Operator may certify the disclosure necessary in the public interest, if it is satisfied of these matters, having had regard to the impact the disclosure might have on me (Rules ss 42, 43(1); Act s 95(1)(a))`
    `no, not under Rules s 43: the information can reasonably be obtained from a source other than the Department and Services Australia (s 43(1)(a))`
    `no, not under Rules s 43: the disclosure is not covered by any of Rules ss 44 to 54A (s 43(1)(b))`
    `no, not under Rules s 43: the disclosure is not to the kind of recipient, or not in the circumstances, that the section for its purpose names`
    `no, not under Rules s 43: there is reasonable ground to believe the person the information is about would not want it disclosed (Rules s 51(c), s 52(1)(c))`
    `no, not under Rules s 43: the recipient has no genuine and legitimate interest connected with the purpose and is not a listed Minister (s 43(1)(c))`

-- Rules s 43(1): "The Operator may certify ... that disclosure of protected information, that relates to a person ..., is
-- necessary in the public interest if the Operator is satisfied that: (a) the information cannot reasonably be obtained
-- from a source other than the Department and the Human Services Department; and (b) the disclosure is covered by any of
-- sections 44 to 54A of this instrument; and (c) the person to whom the information will be disclosed either: (i) has a
-- genuine and legitimate interest in the information connected with the circumstances described in a section covering the
-- disclosure; or (ii) is a Minister covered by subsection (2) of this section." s 42: "the Operator must have regard to the
-- impact the disclosure might have on the person." ss 46, 48, 51 and 54 name the recipient; s 50 a listed Minister;
-- ss 51(c) and 52(1)(c) add "there is no reasonable ground to believe that the [missing or deceased] person would not want
-- the information disclosed". A failed "if": no certificate under s 43 (other disclosures under Act s 95(1)(b) and (1A)
-- are outside the Rules).
@export Can the redress scheme give information about me to someone else because it is in the public interest (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) Part 11)? The Operator may certify a public-interest disclosure only if the information cannot reasonably be got elsewhere, the purpose is one the Rules list (such as law enforcement, a proceeds of crime order, extradition, correcting a mistake, briefing a Minister, a missing or deceased person, research, reparations or aged care means testing), and the recipient has a genuine and legitimate interest or is a listed Minister. The Operator must weigh the impact on you.
GIVEN `the purpose` IS A `The purpose of the disclosure` @desc Why the information would be disclosed: protecting public revenue; an offence against government officers, property or premises; a proceeds of crime or unexplained wealth order; extradition; international criminal assistance; correcting a mistake of fact; briefing a Minister; a missing person; a deceased person; establishing a death; research, statistics or policy; contacting you about a reparation process; aged care means testing; or some other purpose
      `the recipient` IS A `The recipient of the disclosure` @desc Who would receive the information: someone with a genuine and legitimate interest connected with that purpose; a listed Minister (the Minister, the Centrelink Minister, the Prime Minister, a Premier, a Chief Minister, or a State or Territory Minister responsible for redress); or someone else
      `the information can be got from another source` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information can reasonably be obtained from a source other than the Department of Social Services and Services Australia
      `the purpose section's own conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the disclosure meets the conditions of the section for that purpose, including the recipient it names (for example a law enforcement agency for a proceeds of crime order; for a mistake of fact, that the scheme's integrity is at risk or the matter was published)
      `there is reason to think the person would not want it disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a missing or deceased person only: whether there is reasonable ground to believe that the person would not want (or would not have wanted) the information disclosed
GIVETH A `Whether my information can be disclosed in the public interest`
`Can my information be disclosed in the public interest question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the information can be got from another source`
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 43: the information can reasonably be obtained from a source other than the Department and Services Australia (s 43(1)(a))`
           IF `the purpose` EQUALS `some other purpose`
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 43: the disclosure is not covered by any of Rules ss 44 to 54A (s 43(1)(b))`
           IF (NOT `the purpose section's own conditions are met`)
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 43: the disclosure is not to the kind of recipient, or not in the circumstances, that the section for its purpose names`
           IF (`the purpose` EQUALS `locating a missing person, disclosed to a court, coroner, Royal Commission or government authority (Rules s 51)` OR `the purpose` EQUALS `matters about a deceased person (Rules s 52(1))`) AND `there is reason to think the person would not want it disclosed`
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 43: there is reasonable ground to believe the person the information is about would not want it disclosed (Rules s 51(c), s 52(1)(c))`
           IF `the recipient` EQUALS `someone else`
              THEN `no, not under Rules s 43: the recipient has no genuine and legitimate interest connected with the purpose and is not a listed Minister (s 43(1)(c))`
           OTHERWISE `may be certified: the Operator may certify the disclosure necessary in the public interest, if it is satisfied of these matters, having had regard to the impact the disclosure might have on me (Rules ss 42, 43(1); Act s 95(1)(a))`

§§ `My settlement deed (Rules s 71) [only if I signed a release of an institution]`

DECLARE `Whether a term of my settlement can stop me` IS ONE OF
    `no: the term does not have that effect, and is not enforceable so far as it would have it (Rules s 71(2))`
    `Rules s 71 does not apply: the term is not in an agreement or deed under which I released a participating or listed institution from liability for abuse within the scope of the scheme`
    `Rules s 71 does not apply: the term would not prevent or limit my applying for or receiving redress, the institution's liability or payment under the scheme, or disclosure in connection with the scheme`

-- Rules s 71(1): the section "applies to a provision that: (a) is a provision of an agreement or deed, under which a person
-- releases a participating institution or institutions that are listed for a participating jurisdiction under sections 164,
-- 164A, 164B or 164C of the Act from liability for abuse of the person that is within the scope of the scheme; and (b)
-- apart from this section, would have the effect of preventing, prohibiting, limiting or otherwise inhibiting any of the
-- following: (i) the person applying for or receiving redress under the scheme; (ii) the institution ... having a
-- liability, or making a payment, provided for by the Act or this instrument ...; (iii) disclosure by the person or the
-- [institution or jurisdiction], in connection with the operation of the scheme, of information about the abuse, the
-- agreement or deed or a payment made under the agreement or deed." (2): "The provision does not have that effect, and is
-- not enforceable so far as it would have that effect."
@export Can a confidentiality clause or other term of a settlement I signed with an institution stop me applying for redress or telling the scheme about the abuse or the settlement (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 71)? No: a term of a deed or agreement releasing a participating or listed institution from liability for the abuse cannot stop you applying for or receiving redress, stop the institution paying under the scheme, or stop disclosure to the scheme about the abuse, the deed or a payment under it; it is unenforceable to that extent. The rest of the deed is not affected by this rule.
GIVEN `the term is in a deed releasing a participating or listed institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term is in an agreement or deed under which you released a participating institution (or an institution listed for a participating jurisdiction under Act ss 164-164C) from liability for abuse of you that is within the scope of the scheme
      `it would stop or limit my applying for or receiving redress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term would prevent, prohibit, limit or otherwise inhibit you applying for or receiving redress under the scheme
      `it would stop or limit the institution's liability or payment under the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term would prevent or limit the institution (or the participating jurisdiction) having a liability or making a payment under the scheme in connection with the abuse
      `it would stop or limit disclosure to the scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term would prevent or limit disclosure, by you or the institution or jurisdiction, in connection with the scheme, of information about the abuse, the agreement or deed, or a payment under it (for example a confidentiality clause)
GIVETH A `Whether a term of my settlement can stop me`
`Can my settlement deed stop me using the scheme question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the term is in a deed releasing a participating or listed institution`)
              THEN `Rules s 71 does not apply: the term is not in an agreement or deed under which I released a participating or listed institution from liability for abuse within the scope of the scheme`
           IF `it would stop or limit my applying for or receiving redress` OR `it would stop or limit the institution's liability or payment under the scheme` OR `it would stop or limit disclosure to the scheme`
              THEN `no: the term does not have that effect, and is not enforceable so far as it would have it (Rules s 71(2))`
           OTHERWISE `Rules s 71 does not apply: the term would not prevent or limit my applying for or receiving redress, the institution's liability or payment under the scheme, or disclosure in connection with the scheme`

§§ `What I must tell the Operator (Rules Part 14 Division 3)`

DECLARE `Whether I must report my sentence` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing, in the approved form, as soon as practicable after I know of the sentence (Act s 181(1); Rules s 72)`
    `no, not under Act s 181(1): I have not applied for redress`
    `no, not under Act s 181(1): the sentence is less than 5 years`
    `no, not under Act s 181(1): I was sentenced before I applied (Act s 63 still applies to that sentence)`

-- Act s 181(1): "If: (a) a person makes an application for redress under the scheme; and (b) after making the
-- application, the person is sentenced to imprisonment for 5 years or longer for an offence against a law of the
-- Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign country; then the person must notify the Operator of that fact in
-- accordance with any requirements prescribed by the rules." Rules s 72: "the notification must be made in writing in the
-- approved form as soon as practicable after the person knows of the sentence."
@export Must I tell the redress scheme that I have been sentenced to prison, and how (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 72; Act s 181(1))? If, after applying for redress, you are sentenced to imprisonment for 5 years or longer for any offence (in Australia or overseas), you must notify the Operator in writing, in the approved form, as soon as practicable after you know of the sentence.
GIVEN `I have applied for redress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made an application for redress
      `the sentence in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the prison sentence in years (for example 5, or 4.5)
      `I was sentenced after applying` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sentenced after you made your application for redress
GIVETH A `Whether I must report my sentence`
`Must I tell the Operator about my prison sentence question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `I have applied for redress`)
              THEN `no, not under Act s 181(1): I have not applied for redress`
           IF `the sentence in years` LESS THAN 5
              THEN `no, not under Act s 181(1): the sentence is less than 5 years`
           IF (NOT `I was sentenced after applying`)
              THEN `no, not under Act s 181(1): I was sentenced before I applied (Act s 63 still applies to that sentence)`
           OTHERWISE `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing, in the approved form, as soon as practicable after I know of the sentence (Act s 181(1); Rules s 72)`

DECLARE `When I accepted the payment offer` IS ONE OF
    `before I applied for redress`
    `after I applied, before I was given notice of the Operator's determination`
    `after I was given notice approving my application, before I accepted or declined the offer of redress`
    `after I was given notice that my application was not approved`
    `after I accepted the offer of redress`

DECLARE `Whether I must report a payment offer I accepted` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing as soon as practicable, naming the institution by or for which the payment is to be paid (Rules s 73(2), (3))`
    `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing as soon as practicable and in any case before I accept the offer of redress, naming the institution by or for which the payment is to be paid (Rules s 74(2), (3)); the Operator must then revoke its determination (Rules s 17(3)(a))`
    `no longer: I have declined the offer of redress, so Rules s 74(2) and (3) have ceased to apply (s 74(4))`
    `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: the payment is not from or for an institution those sections name, or does not relate to the abuse`
    `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: I did not accept the payment offer in the period those sections cover`

-- Rules s 73(1): applies if "(a) a person has applied for redress under the Act; and (b) before the person is given notice
-- of a determination under section 29 ..., the person accepts an offer of a payment that: (i) is to be paid to the person
-- by, or on behalf of, a participating institution or institutions that are listed for a participating jurisdiction under
-- sections 164, 164A, 164B or 164C of the Act that is identified in the application as being involved in abuse of the
-- person within the scope of the scheme; and (ii) relates to the abuse." (2): "The person must, as soon as practicable,
-- notify the Operator in writing of the person's acceptance of the offer." (3): "The notification must identify the
-- institution ..." s 74(1): applies if "(a) a person is given notice of a determination ... approving the person's
-- application ...; and (b) after the person is given the notice and before the person accepts the offer of redress, the
-- person accepts an offer of a payment that: (i) is to be paid to the person by, or on behalf of, a responsible
-- institution; and (ii) relates to the abuse of the person for which the institution is responsible." (2): "... as soon as
-- practicable and in any case before accepting the offer of redress ..." (4): "Subsections (2) and (3) cease to apply if
-- the person declines the offer of redress."
@export I have accepted an offer of a payment from an institution for the abuse while my redress application is under way: must I tell the Operator, and by when (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) ss 73, 74)? If you accept such an offer after applying and before you are told the decision, from an institution named in your application, you must tell the Operator in writing as soon as practicable. If you accept one after your application is approved and before you accept your offer of redress, from a responsible institution, you must tell the Operator as soon as practicable and before accepting your offer of redress; the Operator must then revoke its decision. The duty ends if you decline the offer of redress.
GIVEN `when I accepted the payment offer` IS A `When I accepted the payment offer` @desc When you accepted the offer of payment: before applying for redress; after applying, before being told the Operator's decision; after being told your application was approved, before accepting or declining the offer of redress; after being told it was not approved; or after accepting the offer of redress
      `the payer is an institution named in my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is to be paid by or for a participating institution (or an institution listed for a participating jurisdiction under Act ss 164-164C) that your application identifies as involved in the abuse
      `the payer is a responsible institution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment is to be paid by or for an institution the Operator has determined is responsible for the abuse
      `the payment relates to the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment relates to the abuse (for which the institution is responsible)
      `I have declined the offer of redress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since declined your offer of redress
GIVETH A `Whether I must report a payment offer I accepted`
`Must I tell the Operator about a payment offer I accepted question` MEANS
    CONSIDER `when I accepted the payment offer`
    WHEN `after I applied, before I was given notice of the Operator's determination` THEN
        IF `the payer is an institution named in my application` AND `the payment relates to the abuse`
        THEN `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing as soon as practicable, naming the institution by or for which the payment is to be paid (Rules s 73(2), (3))`
        ELSE `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: the payment is not from or for an institution those sections name, or does not relate to the abuse`
    WHEN `after I was given notice approving my application, before I accepted or declined the offer of redress` THEN
        IF (NOT (`the payer is a responsible institution` AND `the payment relates to the abuse`))
        THEN `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: the payment is not from or for an institution those sections name, or does not relate to the abuse`
        ELSE IF `I have declined the offer of redress`
             THEN `no longer: I have declined the offer of redress, so Rules s 74(2) and (3) have ceased to apply (s 74(4))`
             ELSE `yes: I must notify the Operator in writing as soon as practicable and in any case before I accept the offer of redress, naming the institution by or for which the payment is to be paid (Rules s 74(2), (3)); the Operator must then revoke its determination (Rules s 17(3)(a))`
    OTHERWISE `no, not under Rules ss 73-74: I did not accept the payment offer in the period those sections cover`

-- Rules s 74(2) as a regulative rule, counted in days from the day I accepted the payment offer (day 0) to the day I
-- accept my offer of redress: I must notify the Operator by then. A notice given on the day I accept the offer of redress
-- is taken as given before it (fork F6). "As soon as practicable" is a judgment for others and is not decided here.
GIVEN `the days until I accept my offer of redress` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Rules party` `Rules step`
`Rules s 74(2) -- I must notify the Operator before I accept my offer of redress` `the days until I accept my offer of redress` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the survivor`
    MUST `notify the Operator in writing that I accepted the payment offer`
    WITHIN `the days until I accept my offer of redress`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the survivor` BECAUSE "I accepted my offer of redress without first notifying the Operator in writing that I had accepted an offer of payment from a responsible institution (Rules s 74(2))"

GIVEN `the days until I accept my offer of redress` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 74(2) -- a notification on this day is in time` `the days until I accept my offer of redress` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`Rules s 74(2) -- I must notify the Operator before I accept my offer of redress` `the days until I accept my offer of redress`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `I, the survivor` `notify the Operator in writing that I accepted the payment offer` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Whether I told the Operator in time` IS ONE OF
    `in time: I notified the Operator before accepting my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`
    `late: I accepted my offer of redress before notifying the Operator (Rules s 74(2))`
    `still due: I must notify the Operator as soon as practicable, and before I accept my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2))`
    `done: I notified the Operator, and have not yet accepted my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`

@export Did I tell the Operator in time that I accepted a payment from a responsible institution, before accepting my offer of redress (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 (Cth) s 74(2))? After your application is approved, a payment offer you accept from a responsible institution must be reported in writing as soon as practicable, and in any case before you accept your offer of redress. Whether you acted "as soon as practicable" is not decided here.
GIVEN `the day I accepted the payment offer` IS A DATE @desc The day you accepted the offer of payment from the responsible institution
      `I have notified the Operator` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Operator in writing that you accepted that payment offer
      `the day I notified the Operator` IS A DATE @desc The day you notified the Operator (any date if you have not)
      `I have accepted my offer of redress` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have accepted your offer of redress
      `the day I accepted my offer of redress` IS A DATE @desc The day you accepted your offer of redress (any date if you have not)
GIVETH A `Whether I told the Operator in time`
`Did I tell the Operator about the payment in time question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I have accepted my offer of redress` AND `I have notified the Operator` AND `Rules s 74(2) -- a notification on this day is in time` (`the days from` `the day I accepted the payment offer` `until` `the day I accepted my offer of redress`) (`the days from` `the day I accepted the payment offer` `until` `the day I notified the Operator`)
              THEN `in time: I notified the Operator before accepting my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`
           IF `I have accepted my offer of redress`
              THEN `late: I accepted my offer of redress before notifying the Operator (Rules s 74(2))`
           IF `I have notified the Operator`
              THEN `done: I notified the Operator, and have not yet accepted my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2)); whether it was as soon as practicable is not decided here`
           OTHERWISE `still due: I must notify the Operator as soon as practicable, and before I accept my offer of redress (Rules s 74(2))`
